PODFoam llm_demo: an observer asking a local vision-language model

python_module.py is an example for the two hooks. At chosen steps it
draws |U| and p and asks a vision-language model on a local llama-server
about them. It records the answer with the arrays; model output never
goes back into the solver. Each request runs in a forked worker with a
deadline, so a slow or dead server cannot hold the solver past it.
run_demo.sh runs five cases, synchronous or asynchronous. verify_demo.py
and verify_async.py check that the written fields equal those of the
same run with no model requests. The unit tests need no solver or model.

